<title>UK: Ghana weekly cocoa purchases drop to 1,893 T.</title>
<headline>Ghana weekly cocoa purchases drop to 1,893 T.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ghana weekly cocoa purchases amounted to 1,983 tonnes in the 21st week of 1996/97 ending March 6 with the cumulative reaching 296,109 tonnes, the Ghana Cocoa Board said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The latest weekly data compares with 2,428 tonnes in the previous week ending February 27.</p>
<p>In the 1995/96 season, purchases ran at 3,666 tonnes in the 21st week which ended on February 29, with the cumulative at 333,175. By March 7, the cumulative was 336,609 tonnes.</p>
<p>-- Clelia Oziel, London Newsroom +44-171-542 8072</p>
